# Environment and test data

## `.env` (never committed)

- Portal URLs (`STAFF_URL`, `VETERAN_URL`, `PROVIDER_URL`) and `<ROLE>_EMAIL` / `<ROLE>_PASSWORD` pairs.
- `.env.example` lists every key with an empty value. Add a key there in the same change that first reads it.
- Read values only through `requireEnv`, `portalUrl` or `credentials`, so a missing key fails as `[automation]`
  with the key's name.
- Shell environment variables override `.env` (useful for CI secrets).

## `TEST_DATA` (committed)

`tests/support/test-data.ts` holds fixed records in the target environment: names, ids, option labels.
These are identifiers, not secrets.

- One entry per record, with a `/** */` saying what it is and which check depends on it.
- Group by record (`veteran`, `provider`, ...). The VETERAN / PROVIDER entries describe the same accounts as
  `.env`; keep them in step when the accounts change.
- Never put emails, phone numbers or passwords here. If a check needs an account's email, use `credentials(role).email`.
- When a record is renamed in the environment, change it here only. A spec that still breaks has an inlined literal; fix that too.

## `.auth/` (never committed)

Written by `tests/auth.setup.ts` on every run. Delete it freely; the next run recreates it.
